The  SecureTTY  service module for PAM provides functionality for
only one PAM category: account management.  In terms of the para‐
meter, this is the feature.  It also provides null functions  for
authentication  and  session  management.   The SecureTTY account
management component returns failure if the user is attempting to
authenticate as superuser, and the process is attached to an  in‐
secure  TTY.   In all other cases, the module returns success.  A
TTY is considered secure if it is listed in and has the flag set.
The following options may be passed to the authentication module:
debugging information at level.  suppress warning messages to the
user.  These messages include reasons why the user’s  authentica‐
tion attempt was declined.
